I hadn't played nethack for a few months or so, so I sat down one evening
and cranked up a good character. A Knight, 17th level or so, had basically
all the intrinsics EXCEPT teleport control (boy, do I regret that now), AC
-29! (+1 Black DSM, +3 Cloak of Mag. Res, +4 Shield of Refl, +3 helm of
brilliance, +7 & +4 Rings of protection, +2 leather gloves, and some
shoes). I had a +5 Excalibur, and pretty much slew everything in a few
blows.

Hearing the good news in the castle level that ``The wizard of Yendor is
below your feet'', I figured I'd take him right now. Originally, I planned
to max out my stats and get some other good Armor (I had St: 18/45, but the
other stats were not so hot).

For a while, I was whaling on the guy, getting him down to 36 hit points.
(I had a stethoscope too :-)) Then he teleported away, and when I saw him
again, he split into *TWO* wizards, and summoned some pets... I guess I
should have taken evasive action earlier, but oh well. Finally, reading a
scroll of teleport while confused, I got back a few levels up, but he
followed me, tracked me down, and with ten HP left (but still my fabulous
AC of -29), I saw this happen:

The invisible Wizard of Yendor hits--more--(of course, that didn't make any
difference, I was invisible and had the intrinsic see invisible)

Alas:

 No  Points     Name                                                   Hp [max]
  1     383569  K++-K died on dungeon level 20 [max 29].               -   [80]
                Killed by the invisible Wizard of Yendor.


I guess the moral of this story is, don't get too brazen, and don't
powertype on the Wizard of Yendor...

Some other weird things that happened which I didn't realize was possible
is that the wizard cursed my unicorn horn, and when I applied it I became
sick. And my Excalibur even became cursed! Is there any way to be protected
from people cursing you? Apparently it doesn't fall under magic
resistance...

